            <ArticleTitle>Post-coital haemoperitoneum: a downside to intercourse.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e26-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1308/003588412X13171221499586</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 43-year-old multiparous female patient presenting with post-coital haemoperitoneum secondary to a ruptured uterine fibroid. This is a rare case demonstrating the need to elicit full gynaecological history in patients presenting with an acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
